(1577700, 211816, 39850, '<td valign="top">''8'' - Nice shot.  I can''t tell if it is the light on the water or the lighting is as a result of the long exposure, but I like the effect it has on that main stream.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); This is just a fraction dark in my opinion, I would love to see that green, especially in the foreground really stand out ''luminously''.  The colors are simple though and that is nice.  I wondered when I first looked at this whether it may have looked better (in my opinion) if it were cropped to remove that far left ''stream''.. not sure.  Also, the top of the fall included, perhaps, if it is any good, but that would likely change the whole photograph.  It portrays a ''cold feel'' (as in temperature) in my opinion.  Nice capture of the location.</td>', '''8'' - Nice shot.  I can''t tell if it is the light on the water or the lighting is as a result of the long exposure, but I like the effect it has on that main stream.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); This is just a fraction dark in my opinion, I would love to see that green, especially in the foreground really stand out ''luminously''.  The colors are simple though and that is nice.  I wondered when I first looked at this whether it may have looked better (in my opinion) if it were cropped to remove that far left ''stream''.. not sure.  Also, the top of the fall included, perhaps, if it is any good, but that would likely change the whole photograph.  It portrays a ''cold feel'' (as in temperature) in my opinion.  Nice capture of the location.', '2005-08-01 08:41:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577704, 210947, 33352, '<td valign="top">Hard to work out your point of vision, it looks as if you were in a car,as all the lights appear to be comming at you, but IMO....9</td>', 'Hard to work out your point of vision, it looks as if you were in a car,as all the lights appear to be comming at you, but IMO....9', '2005-08-01 08:43:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577706, 210121, 33352, '<td valign="top">Lke the textures in this,and the stance of the subject...9</td>', 'Lke the textures in this,and the stance of the subject...9', '2005-08-01 08:45:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577709, 210983, 16241, '<td valign="top">awesome angle</td>', 'awesome angle', '2005-08-01 08:48:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577711, 211872, 16241, '<td valign="top">howdy pardner</td>', 'howdy pardner', '2005-08-01 08:49:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577715, 211798, 39850, '<td valign="top">''7'' - I like the concept of this, even without the ''couple''.. now that I think of that I think this would be a better photograph without couple, in my opinion.  Because, that angle you have and the size of the fall and the cliff face etc, makes for a very ahh ''mammoth'', almost ''looming'' kind of feel.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); whilst I do like the colors, perhaps more contrasting on the pebbles, or again, an even tighter (ground level) angle, to incorporate ''some'' of the pebbles, giving even more perspective, would make this a better photograph in my opinion.  Just if you were able to get that green on the cliff face a little ''bolder'', and the gray of the pebbles, would make it a more dramatic shot in my opinion.  As for the shot as it is (with the couple, and that ''dreaming'' theme to fit with your idea for the Challenge), my first thoughts were that the blue jacket was not subtle like ''hers'' and therefore detracts from the mood and feel of this photograph.  In this instance, perhaps b/w would have worked better.  The concept is a nice one though and does have a romantic type feel.. the only other criticism would be with the male, in his ''solo left'' shot, he is looking at the camera and I think if he were looking at her (as she seems to be looking at him?), it would have made this a better photograph in my opinion.</td>', '''7'' - I like the concept of this, even without the ''couple''.. now that I think of that I think this would be a better photograph without couple, in my opinion.  Because, that angle you have and the size of the fall and the cliff face etc, makes for a very ahh ''mammoth'', almost ''looming'' kind of feel.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); whilst I do like the colors, perhaps more contrasting on the pebbles, or again, an even tighter (ground level) angle, to incorporate ''some'' of the pebbles, giving even more perspective, would make this a better photograph in my opinion.  Just if you were able to get that green on the cliff face a little ''bolder'', and the gray of the pebbles, would make it a more dramatic shot in my opinion.  As for the shot as it is (with the couple, and that ''dreaming'' theme to fit with your idea for the Challenge), my first thoughts were that the blue jacket was not subtle like ''hers'' and therefore detracts from the mood and feel of this photograph.  In this instance, perhaps b/w would have worked better.  The concept is a nice one though and does have a romantic type feel.. the only other criticism would be with the male, in his ''solo left'' shot, he is looking at the camera and I think if he were looking at her (as she seems to be looking at him?), it would have made this a better photograph in my opinion.', '2005-08-01 08:50:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577718, 210057, 16241, '<td valign="top">this is awesome!  curtain of light, looks like a bride.  square format is great.<br/></td>', 'this is awesome!  curtain of light, looks like a bride.  square format is great.', '2005-08-01 08:52:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577723, 211793, 16241, '<td valign="top">very good</td>', 'very good', '2005-08-01 08:54:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577724, 211855, 39850, '<td valign="top">''7'' - This is a good concept and has a lot of potential.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); my first thoughts on seeing this was that I would like to have seen the far right ''edge'' incorporated.  Cropping out of the windows/signs? up middle through top right would make this a better photograph in my opinion.  Also, I think a slight nudge rotation to the left to align it better is required.  As far as I know this is an advanced editing Challenge, so I would like to see those ''things'' in between the first and second fore spouts removed.  Seems to be a fraction of gamma trouble with some black areas on the water, but that MAY be my monitor.  I think the b/w(?) works well here.</td>', '''7'' - This is a good concept and has a lot of potential.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); my first thoughts on seeing this was that I would like to have seen the far right ''edge'' incorporated.  Cropping out of the windows/signs? up middle through top right would make this a better photograph in my opinion.  Also, I think a slight nudge rotation to the left to align it better is required.  As far as I know this is an advanced editing Challenge, so I would like to see those ''things'' in between the first and second fore spouts removed.  Seems to be a fraction of gamma trouble with some black areas on the water, but that MAY be my monitor.  I think the b/w(?) works well here.', '2005-08-01 08:54:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577735, 211760, 16241, '<td valign="top">great shot!</td>', 'great shot!', '2005-08-01 09:01:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577740, 211548, 20066, '<td valign="top">would have liked it more if croped more.  But goog anyway as it is.</td>', 'would have liked it more if croped more.  But goog anyway as it is.', '2005-08-01 09:05:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577743, 211806, 20066, '<td valign="top">i like this colors a lot!</td>', 'i like this colors a lot!', '2005-08-01 09:06:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577772, 211500, 39850, '<td valign="top">''8'' - Very nice shot.  I just noticed the ''drifts'' at the bottom (look like smoke) and at the top (smaller works?) that you have captured, never seen that before in a fireworks shot.  Nice perspective.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); at first glance it looked like the water''s edge was a fraction higher on the right, but on closer inspection it seemed to balance out to my eye(s).  On looking again now the same thing though, it may be the ships(?) in the very right of the frame doing it, not sure.  Perhaps this shot might be even more dramatic with even less water, not sure.  For me, even a darker sky/city contrast would make this a better photograph in my opinion.</td>', '''8'' - Very nice shot.  I just noticed the ''drifts'' at the bottom (look like smoke) and at the top (smaller works?) that you have captured, never seen that before in a fireworks shot.  Nice perspective.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); at first glance it looked like the water''s edge was a fraction higher on the right, but on closer inspection it seemed to balance out to my eye(s).  On looking again now the same thing though, it may be the ships(?) in the very right of the frame doing it, not sure.  Perhaps this shot might be even more dramatic with even less water, not sure.  For me, even a darker sky/city contrast would make this a better photograph in my opinion.', '2005-08-01 09:28:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577781, 209697, 39850, '<td valign="top">''8'' - Very nice ah, ''composition'', nice crisp clean feel.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); firstly, for me, I don''t like the texture on that ball (looks plastic to me), nor the color in this scheme.  I wonder if some variation on the colors may have given more impact to this shot.  No idea how you made the ''streaks'', but they look very good.  Again, the blue and brown, actually work ok together here, but for me, in my opinion, they clash with the central subject, thus it detracts a lot from this image.  Very simple feel though, I like it.</td>', '''8'' - Very nice ah, ''composition'', nice crisp clean feel.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); firstly, for me, I don''t like the texture on that ball (looks plastic to me), nor the color in this scheme.  I wonder if some variation on the colors may have given more impact to this shot.  No idea how you made the ''streaks'', but they look very good.  Again, the blue and brown, actually work ok together here, but for me, in my opinion, they clash with the central subject, thus it detracts a lot from this image.  Very simple feel though, I like it.', '2005-08-01 09:33:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577787, 209155, 24920, '<td valign="top">I like this composition, the perspective, and the sepia tone. Perhaps the face should have not overlapped with an element in the background...</td>', 'I like this composition, the perspective, and the sepia tone. Perhaps the face should have not overlapped with an element in the background...', '2005-08-01 09:38:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577788, 210821, 39850, '<td valign="top">''7'' - Nice shot.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures);  whilst I am a fan of this type of shot, I am wondering if perhaps there was a little too much exposure as there seems to be almost a ''slime'' feel to this.  I know you have worked your title into that feel, and while it does look in parts like ''melting'', for me, especially without the title, it has a different ''feel''.  The colors are nice, but I would like to see them even bolder (the green especially).  Also, I favor that left hand side of the photograph and if that (dependent of course what is further left) were more in frame, it would make this a better photograph in my opinion, especially if you were able to capture more of the texture (and you already have) of the moss etc.  That ''hanging'' at the left rear and the seemingly ''still'' water there looks intriguing.</td>', '''7'' - Nice shot.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures);  whilst I am a fan of this type of shot, I am wondering if perhaps there was a little too much exposure as there seems to be almost a ''slime'' feel to this.  I know you have worked your title into that feel, and while it does look in parts like ''melting'', for me, especially without the title, it has a different ''feel''.  The colors are nice, but I would like to see them even bolder (the green especially).  Also, I favor that left hand side of the photograph and if that (dependent of course what is further left) were more in frame, it would make this a better photograph in my opinion, especially if you were able to capture more of the texture (and you already have) of the moss etc.  That ''hanging'' at the left rear and the seemingly ''still'' water there looks intriguing.', '2005-08-01 09:39:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577790, 211849, 39850, '<td valign="top">''8'' - This is a great shot - makes me want to hold onto the desk for stability.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); Difficult, but as I am sure you are aware, if there was perfect focus/sharpness on the handlebars at least, would make this ''pop out'' even more than it does. Really that is about all I can say, other than perhaps a slight nudge rotation to the right, just a fraction.  Must be a dink/tandem with the rider leant to the side(?), you did very well to get it centered. The colors are really great, love that green.. well done.</td>', '''8'' - This is a great shot - makes me want to hold onto the desk for stability.  Criticism (with the caveat I know squat about long exposures); Difficult, but as I am sure you are aware, if there was perfect focus/sharpness on the handlebars at least, would make this ''pop out'' even more than it does. Really that is about all I can say, other than perhaps a slight nudge rotation to the right, just a fraction.  Must be a dink/tandem with the rider leant to the side(?), you did very well to get it centered. The colors are really great, love that green.. well done.', '2005-08-01 09:42:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577794, 211758, 21714, '<td valign="top">Always enjoy shots like this. Nice.</td>', 'Always enjoy shots like this. Nice.', '2005-08-01 09:47:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577795, 210979, 24920, '<td valign="top">Great shot. The car fits well in the composition and makes it unusual.</td>', 'Great shot. The car fits well in the composition and makes it unusual.', '2005-08-01 09:49:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577798, 211558, 24920, '<td valign="top">Dramatic, powerful effect.</td>', 'Dramatic, powerful effect.', '2005-08-01 09:51:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577799, 210057, 27763, '<td valign="top">Wow!  This is really good.  I like this a lot.</td>', 'Wow!  This is really good.  I like this a lot.', '2005-08-01 09:52:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577800, 210738, 21714, '<td valign="top">Love the use of colours and the seperation in this one. Well done.</td>', 'Love the use of colours and the seperation in this one. Well done.', '2005-08-01 09:53:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577808, 210804, 15711, '<td valign="top">Good lighting and the golden tones created by the long expsoure are very appealing to the eye. I like the perpendicular in juxtaposition with the horizontal lines of the bridge. Nicely shot. Interesting perspective as well. Are those smoke stacks?? I wish they were bathed in light as well as the other two and the bridge, but you can''t always adjust Mother Nature now can you?</td>', 'Good lighting and the golden tones created by the long expsoure are very appealing to the eye. I like the perpendicular in juxtaposition with the horizontal lines of the bridge. Nicely shot. Interesting perspective as well. Are those smoke stacks?? I wish they were bathed in light as well as the other two and the bridge, but you can''t always adjust Mother Nature now can you?', '2005-08-01 09:57:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577811, 211313, 15711, '<td valign="top">Oh the notes make the shot.  I love the soft diffused feeling and the blue tones are great here. I''ve just reconsidered this on 2nd view and I''m upping it to a 10.  I think everything about it is so appealing and certainly artful in all respects.  Greatly composed and executed. (applause)</td>', 'Oh the notes make the shot.  I love the soft diffused feeling and the blue tones are great here. I''ve just reconsidered this on 2nd view and I''m upping it to a 10.  I think everything about it is so appealing and certainly artful in all respects.  Greatly composed and executed. (applause)', '2005-08-01 09:59:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577814, 211306, 15711, '<td valign="top">Really smart use of light. I like the softness without blurriness. The green is appealing and casts a nice glow on the white tee shirt. Upon second review, I''m upping it to a 9.  Way to go!!</td>', 'Really smart use of light. I like the softness without blurriness. The green is appealing and casts a nice glow on the white tee shirt. Upon second review, I''m upping it to a 9.  Way to go!!', '2005-08-01 10:01:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577816, 211199, 15711, '<td valign="top">Of all the trailing lights, I think this is my favorite.  It is a leading line to the utmost degree. I love the red and white in its impactful simplicity.  8</td>', 'Of all the trailing lights, I think this is my favorite.  It is a leading line to the utmost degree. I love the red and white in its impactful simplicity.  8', '2005-08-01 10:03:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577819, 211886, 37719, '<td valign="top">I like the idea but wish you didn''t use the border.</td>', 'I like the idea but wish you didn''t use the border.', '2005-08-01 10:04:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577822, 211214, 15711, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8 without hesitation and upon 2nd review, I''m sticking to it. The colors are lovely and the circular quality amidst the angular rocks and logs is really a nice overlayed effect. This would make a great poster!!</td>', 'I gave this an 8 without hesitation and upon 2nd review, I''m sticking to it. The colors are lovely and the circular quality amidst the angular rocks and logs is really a nice overlayed effect. This would make a great poster!!', '2005-08-01 10:05:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577823, 211479, 15711, '<td valign="top">All of the elements coming out of the water here and there make for great composition. They lead your eye right to the back - the lighthouse.  The rocks are so vivid and clear and the water has a serene softness due to the time of day.  Nice all the way around.</td>', 'All of the elements coming out of the water here and there make for great composition. They lead your eye right to the back - the lighthouse.  The rocks are so vivid and clear and the water has a serene softness due to the time of day.  Nice all the way around.', '2005-08-01 10:06:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577827, 210136, 15711, '<td valign="top">My only critique is that I''m not crazy about the funky green filter.  But the shot is well done and I like your perspective on the shot. 7</td>', 'My only critique is that I''m not crazy about the funky green filter.  But the shot is well done and I like your perspective on the shot. 7', '2005-08-01 10:08:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577829, 211787, 15711, '<td valign="top">Lots of waterfalls and this is a really good example. The rich greens are a nice contrast to the velvety white falls.</td>', 'Lots of waterfalls and this is a really good example. The rich greens are a nice contrast to the velvety white falls.', '2005-08-01 10:09:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577831, 209838, 15711, '<td valign="top">If it were in a beaker, I''d think I was in 4th grade science. hee hee  This is effective and the contrast of the red and white is nicely done.  I think the crop is a tad tight and I would have liked to see this off centered with more negative space.</td>', 'If it were in a beaker, I''d think I was in 4th grade science. hee hee  This is effective and the contrast of the red and white is nicely done.  I think the crop is a tad tight and I would have liked to see this off centered with more negative space.', '2005-08-01 10:10:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577832, 210057, 15711, '<td valign="top">Great silhouette and sense of movement. I like the leading lines aspect of it as well.</td>', 'Great silhouette and sense of movement. I like the leading lines aspect of it as well.', '2005-08-01 10:11:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1577833, 211756, 15711, '<td valign="top">Very pretty. Love all of the colors and their "strings" of light.  Nicely done.</td>', 'Very pretty. Love all of the colors and their "strings" of light.  Nicely done.', '2005-08-01 10:11:48.000000', NULL, 1),
