(1593619, 211896, 41522, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!!!  I was one of the 50 to rate this 10.  As one of your other comments mentioned, I also think of Wuthering Heights when I view this.  It has a great mood and is very deserving of the recognition.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-08 01:20:12.</i></td>', 'Congratulations!!!  I was one of the 50 to rate this 10.  As one of your other comments mentioned, I also think of Wuthering Heights when I view this.  It has a great mood and is very deserving of the recognition.', '2005-08-08 01:56:44.000000', '2005-08-08 02:20:12.000000', 0),
(1593621, 211169, 4281, '<td valign="top">LOL, yet another 4th place!<br/>It''s a bit funny that I''ve entered into 4 challenges on DPC in July and in 3 of those I ended up in the 4th place. In addition, I''ve also entered into 3 challenges in July at another photography contest site here in Iceland and I also ended up in the 4th place in all of those challenges. So in all, I''ve entered into 7 challenges in July and the 4th place was mine in all but one of those instances. Guess I can''t complain, can I? ;-)<br/> <br/>Anyway, thanks for all the comments folks!<br/>I especially want to answer skief who complaimed about grainyness in the top-left corner. This isn''t really noise/grain but tiny water droplets coming from the waterfall.<br/>As for the title, which JohannesFrank commented on, it refers to the fact that this is a one second exposure.<br/> <br/>I''d like to thank Larus for inviting me on this trip to Gullfoss (well, I bought him a sandwich instead) and for lending me the ND-filter. <br/> <br/>If anyone is curious, this waterfall, Gullfoss, is one the most well known tourist attractions in Iceland. Pictures of it can be easily found on the Internet.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-08 01:09:19.</i></td>', 'LOL, yet another 4th place!It''s a bit funny that I''ve entered into 4 challenges on DPC in July and in 3 of those I ended up in the 4th place. In addition, I''ve also entered into 3 challenges in July at another photography contest site here in Iceland and I also ended up in the 4th place in all of those challenges. So in all, I''ve entered into 7 challenges in July and the 4th place was mine in all but one of those instances. Guess I can''t complain, can I? ;-) Anyway, thanks for all the comments folks!I especially want to answer skief who complaimed about grainyness in the top-left corner. This isn''t really noise/grain but tiny water droplets coming from the waterfall.As for the title, which JohannesFrank commented on, it refers to the fact that this is a one second exposure. I''d like to thank Larus for inviting me on this trip to Gullfoss (well, I bought him a sandwich instead) and for lending me the ND-filter.  If anyone is curious, this waterfall, Gullfoss, is one the most well known tourist attractions in Iceland. Pictures of it can be easily found on the Internet.', '2005-08-08 01:57:27.000000', '2005-08-08 02:09:19.000000', 0),
(1593629, 210738, 24976, '<td valign="top">Congrats Justin! Its nice to see one of us young-uns in the top 5 :-)<br/> <br/>Seriously we need to form some sort of group for all the dpc-ers under 21... some quick names i can think of are you, me, zoomdak (thomas), joey, konador (ben), nightshy, tranquil and annah.</td>', 'Congrats Justin! Its nice to see one of us young-uns in the top 5 :-) Seriously we need to form some sort of group for all the dpc-ers under 21... some quick names i can think of are you, me, zoomdak (thomas), joey, konador (ben), nightshy, tranquil and annah.', '2005-08-08 02:00:19.000000', NULL, 0),
