(1595062, 211785, 20530, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for the great comments.<br/> <br/>I wasn''t going to enter this, but someone talked me into it. Glad I did, as it is currently my 2nd highest score.<br/> <br/>The original had a great deal of noise. This is the first time I''ve used Noise Ninja. Not sure I used it correctly, but it did help considerably.<br/>Thanks again to <a href="//dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30861" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Bear_music</a> for pointers on editing, and convincing me to enter it.<br/> <br/>The horizon appears to be slanted, but this is an optical illusion. It''s almost impossible to identify the actual horizon as it actually conisists of two different islands. I think the lack of lights on the left contributes to this illusion.<br/> <br/>I flip-flopped on cropping out the bird. Do wish it were larger and more in focus.</td>', 'Thanks everyone for the great comments. I wasn''t going to enter this, but someone talked me into it. Glad I did, as it is currently my 2nd highest score. The original had a great deal of noise. This is the first time I''ve used Noise Ninja. Not sure I used it correctly, but it did help considerably.Thanks again to Bear_music for pointers on editing, and convincing me to enter it. The horizon appears to be slanted, but this is an optical illusion. It''s almost impossible to identify the actual horizon as it actually conisists of two different islands. I think the lack of lights on the left contributes to this illusion. I flip-flopped on cropping out the bird. Do wish it were larger and more in focus.', '2005-08-08 13:44:29.000000', NULL, 0),
