(1597776, 211792, 18319, '<td valign="top">Nice picture living in Buffalo,NY most of the my younger life I knew the view right away. I do have to ask did you do a little color inhancement. I thought you might have because I don''t remember the colors always being so vibrant. I also would have given it a ten had I been able to vote. I now live in Richmond Va so seeing the falls lit up my day. Best of luck.<br/>   LennyV<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-09 12:00:01.</i></td>', 'Nice picture living in Buffalo,NY most of the my younger life I knew the view right away. I do have to ask did you do a little color inhancement. I thought you might have because I don''t remember the colors always being so vibrant. I also would have given it a ten had I been able to vote. I now live in Richmond Va so seeing the falls lit up my day. Best of luck.   LennyV', '2005-08-09 12:59:04.000000', '2005-08-09 13:00:01.000000', 0),
(1597797, 211792, 12160, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fotologjpw:</b></div><hr/><i> Kudos on the exquisite framing and extraordinary attention to light in this famous shot.<br/> <br/>One problem: the location you cite is Niagara Falls, Ontario (where you were) . . . but of course the subject as presented is entirely Niagara Falls, New York, USA.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.fotolog.net/jpw" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.fotolog.net/jpw</a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comment. You are indeed right, it''s the American Falls that I referred to as the Rainbow Falls. I was closer to the Canadian Falls (the Horseshoe) but the illumination wasn''t as good as in the American Falls.<br/> <br/>Thanks too for marking it as favorite. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by fotologjpw: Kudos on the exquisite framing and extraordinary attention to light in this famous shot. One problem: the location you cite is Niagara Falls, Ontario (where you were) . . . but of course the subject as presented is entirely Niagara Falls, New York, USA. //www.fotolog.net/jpw   Thanks for your comment. You are indeed right, it''s the American Falls that I referred to as the Rainbow Falls. I was closer to the Canadian Falls (the Horseshoe) but the illumination wasn''t as good as in the American Falls. Thanks too for marking it as favorite. :)', '2005-08-09 13:10:14.000000', NULL, 0),
