(4221347, 211785, 67579, '<td valign="top">I couldn''t agree more with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=64571" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Sunshyne</a> that you have a unique way of looking at the world around you and I for one find it inspirational to a degree :) I really like this one, has almost a sense of calmness and power at the same time for me anyway. Great job girl :)<br/> <br/>-dave</td>', 'I couldn''t agree more with  Sunshyne that you have a unique way of looking at the world around you and I for one find it inspirational to a degree :) I really like this one, has almost a sense of calmness and power at the same time for me anyway. Great job girl :) -dave', '2007-11-04 22:43:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4527637, 209997, 52115, '<td valign="top">I used to have a F-717, got one 15th place shot.<br/>It''s a good camera. A tripod, box, , shelf/countertop, or a stack of books for camera support would''ve helped the long exposure. Then set the camera on timer-mode.</td>', 'I used to have a F-717, got one 15th place shot.It''s a good camera. A tripod, box, , shelf/countertop, or a stack of books for camera support would''ve helped the long exposure. Then set the camera on timer-mode.', '2008-02-29 10:10:00.000000', NULL, 0),
